  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n\n// Uses\n\nThe desk, the editor and the rest. \n\nPeople ask, so here is the list. Nothing on it is sponsored, and most of it is older than you would expect.\n\nThe stack, with years\n01\nHardware\n5 items\n14-inch laptop, 36 GB\nThree years old and still faster than any build I give it. I will replace it when the battery gives up.\n27-inch 5K display\nOne screen, not two. Text is sharp enough to read diffs for hours.\nMid-range Android phone\nThe test device. If the site is fast on this, it is fast.\nSplit mechanical keyboard\nLinear switches, blank keycaps. It took a month to get my speed back.\nVertical mouse\nWrists first. I use it for design files and nothing else.\n02\nEditor\n4 items\nVS Code\nMinimap off, sidebar on the right, format on save. Fewer than fifteen extensions.\nJetBrains Mono, 13 px\nThe same typeface as the labels on this site. Ligatures off.\nA dark theme I maintain\nLow contrast for the chrome, full contrast for the code. It lives in the lab.\nGhostty and zsh\nA plain prompt: directory, branch, exit code. Everything else is an alias.\nEditor config\nsettings.json\nCopy\n{\n\n  // the whole list; everything else is the default\n\n  \"editor.fontFamily\": \"JetBrains Mono\",\n\n  \"editor.fontSize\": 13,\n\n  \"editor.fontLigatures\": false,\n\n  \"editor.formatOnSave\": true,\n\n  \"editor.minimap.enabled\": false,\n\n  \"workbench.sideBar.location\": \"right\",\n\n  \"typescript.preferences.importModuleSpecifier\": \"non-relative\"\n\n}\n\n03\nApps\n5 items\nFigma\nFor reading design files and pushing tokens back into them.\nLinear\nIssues written as outcomes, one per pull request.\nObsidian\nPlain markdown notes. Every project gets one decisions file.\nWebPageTest and Lighthouse CI\nA budget the build enforces, and a filmstrip when it fails.\nRaycast\nClipboard history, window halves and a script that opens the right repository.\n04\nDesk\n4 items\nStanding desk, 160 cm\nUp for calls and reviews, down for anything that needs thinking.\nA chair that was worth it\nBought used from an office that closed. The best money on this list.\nOpen-back headphones\nNo noise cancelling; the office is quiet and I like hearing the door.\nA paper notebook, dot grid\nLayouts get drawn here before any file is opened.\n\nLast checked in October 2026. Nothing here is sponsored and none of the links are affiliate links.\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n--:--\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.",
